&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Support analysis of product data to help identify trends, patterns, and opportunities for improvement, under guidance from senior team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Help build and maintain reports and dashboards to track key performance indicators (KPIs) and product metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insights Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist in producing insights and recommendations for stakeholders (Product team, Technology team, Customer team, etc.) based on data analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with product managers, engineers, central analytics team and other stakeholders to understand business needs and help translate them into analytical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Help ensure the accuracy and integrity of data used for analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool Utilization:&lt;/strong&gt; Learn and use analytical tools such as Mixpanel and Dataiku to support data-driven decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate data findings clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, with support from senior colleagues as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor&#39;s degree in Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Business Analytics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Some experience (including internships or academic projects) in product analysis or a related area is a plus; strong potential and eagerness to learn are equally valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Basic proficiency in SQL and Excel; familiarity with data visualization tools such as Mixpanel or Dataiku is a plus. Exposure to Python is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Good analytical and problem-solving skills, with a willingness to develop the ability to translate data into actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Good written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present findings clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attention to Detail:&lt;/strong&gt; Careful and detail-oriented, with a commitment to data accuracy and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable working in a cross-functional team environment and eager to learn from others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Mixpanel or other data visualization tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic knowledge of statistical analysis concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in product management principles and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
