y, including the leadership team, and must have prior Workday HCM configuration experience and deep Workday architecture familiarity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is 100% remote with the option to work at any of our local offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in People Team Leadership meetings (and others as needed) to ensure clear communication relative to project timelines, deliverables and cross-functional dependencies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical and functional leadership for the exploration, evaluation, recommendation, design, and configuration of new features and functionalities within Workday, and other ancillary systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with leaders from the People Team, Finance, IT, and other stakeholders to gather system requirements and translate them into effective Workday solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, test, validate, and implement changes in Workday, ensuring the overall integrity of the Workday platform and that all components of the technical architecture are properly integrated and maintained&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain the documentation of systems related procedures and processes; develop user guides as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and develop a team of analysts, setting objectives that align with team and company strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement HRIS best practices and identify automation opportunities within key business processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and adhere to public company ready ITGC’s as well as best practice business process controls within the People Systems landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who you are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of configuration experience with Workday HCM including business process framework, security, and general system administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years leading an HRIS team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in at least three additional Workday functional areas (Advanced Compensation, Benefits, Absence, Talent &amp;amp; Performance, Time Tracking, Payroll etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess a mastery of report writing, calculated fields, and EIBs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage competing priorities, solve problems quickly, and work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent Communication Skills:&amp;nbsp; Ability to concisely explain complex cross-functional processes. Ability to create clear/simple documentation - process guides &amp;amp; diagrams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with the ability to lead and drive system implementation and enhancement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to evaluate new vendors/products that can bring meaningful ROI on behalf of the organization (particularly related to GenAI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preference given to candidates based within the EST timezone, but open to the CST timezone for the right candidate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday consulting experience a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and troubleshooting Workday integrations (XLSTs, Core Connectors, Studio, RaaS, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with maintaining/updating payroll/equity integrations (e.g. ADP/Deel, and Shareworks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Greenhouse ATS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global public organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SOX compliance / ITGC’s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and/or experience with data visualization, GenAI, and iPass solutions are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to architect multi-step AI workflows that automate Workday and HR processes end-to-end (e.g., onboarding orchestration, policy Q&amp;amp;A, document generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build or govern Claude, Gemini, Workato, GPT-based plugins, or similar tools embedded in HRIS workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data privacy guardrails, bias risk in AI-assisted decisions (compensation, performance), auditability of AI outputs in a SOX-adjacent and Global compliance environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
